1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,460
You can hand a video to a

2
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:03,100
coding agent and get a real edit

3
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:03,380
back.

4
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:05,420
What makes it work is a loop,

5
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:06,540
not a lucky prompt.

6
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,560
Step one is Transcribe.

7
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:12,790
Every word gets a timestamp, so every

8
00:00:12,790 --> 00:00:14,490
graphic can land on the word it

9
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:15,070
belongs to.

10
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,640
Step two is Cut.

11
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,700
Dead air, filler, and retakes come

12
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,780
out, and every cut lands in silence.

13
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:26,210
Step three is Plan the Beats.

14
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:28,550
Each graphic gets a word to land

15
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:30,730
on, a place on screen, and a

16
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:31,410
reason to exist.

17
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:33,870
Step four is Build.

18
00:00:34,490 --> 00:00:36,410
The agent writes the motion as a

19
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:38,030
web page and renders it frame by

20
00:00:38,030 --> 00:00:38,290
frame.

21
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,820
Step five is Verify.

22
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:43,920
It measures the loudness, checks every

23
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:46,260
cut and every card, and fixes what

24
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:47,480
fails before you watch.

25
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:50,020
Then the loop feeds itself.

26
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:52,340
What you liked and what you didn't

27
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:54,400
goes back into the skills, so the

28
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,580
next edit starts smarter.

